    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0573" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v04/pg548"/>

                <head>117. Note From President Carter to Secretary of Defense Brown and the
                    President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs (Brzezinski)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d117-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1979-04-03">April 3,
                    1979</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>To Harold, Zbig</p>
                <p>a) What is status of the assessment of truck mounted mobile launchers for ICBM? Who is doing this analysis?</p>
                <p>b) What is status of negotiation with SU re prior
                    notice of ICBM test launches? What type of
                    tests is included?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                    >J.C.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d117-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d117-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material, Agency
                    File, Box 5, Defense Department: 3–4/79. Secret. Brzezinski forwarded the
                    handwritten note to Brown under an April 3 covering memorandum, in which he
                    noted that his staff and Brown’s staff should “coordinate a prompt reply to the
                    President’s questions.” (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
